Algorithm 1: Depth Oscillation Contour Extraction with Word Count Penalty:
Step 1: Input: thread_data = {comments}, thresholds (20, 50), transition step 0.5
Step 2: Output: contour_points = [(d̃, p)], where d̃ = penalized depth, p = position
Step 3: Initialize contour_points ← ∅
Step 4: Initialize position_counter p ← 0
Step 5: for each top-level comment c in thread_data.comments do
Step 6:  	TraverseVertically(c, base_depth = 0)
Step 7: end for
Procedure TraverseVertically(comment, base_depth)
Step 8:     w ← CountWords(comments.body)
Step 9:     λ ← WordCountPenalty(w)
Step 10:    d̃ ← base_depth × λ
Step 11:    Append(contour_points, (d̃, p))
Step 12:    p ← p + 1
Step 13:    if comment.replies ≠ ∅ then
Step 14:        d_tr ← d̃ + (0.5 × λ)
Step 15:        Append(contour_points, (d_tr, p))
Step 16:        p ← p + 0.5
Step 17:        for each reply r in comment.replies do
Step 18:            TraverseVertically(r, base_depth + 1)
Step 19:        end for
Step 20:        Append(contour_points, (d_tr, p))
Step 21:        p ← p + 0.5
Step 22:    end if
End procedure
Function WordCountPenalty(w)
Step 23:    If w ≥ 50 then return 1.0
Step 24:    Else if 20 ≤ w < 50 then return 0.7 + (w − 20) × (0.3 / 30)
Step 25:    Else return 0.4 + (w / 20) × 0.3
End function

Function CountWords(text)
Step 26:    If text is empty then return 0
Step 27:    Return number of whitespace-separated tokens in text
End function
